\par\par \b \uc2 Food Prices Seen Pushing Up Peru's Inflation in September -  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2012\par 21:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says food prices to keep inflation up in September\par \par \uc2 --Supply pressures on food prices are seen easing in October\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Ryan Dube \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday higher food prices are expected to push up Peru's consumer price index in September, however the inflation rate should still converge to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target range by the end of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In August, consumer prices in Peru rose 0.51% from the previous month, bringing the 12-month inflation rate to 3.53%. The increase, which was higher-than-expected, was largely due to supply factors that boosted prices for perishable foods, like lemons and onions, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This increase in the price of foods affected the month of August, and it is also going to affect the month of September," the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's chief economist, Adrian Armas, said during a conference call with reporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Armas said that Peru's CPI is forecast to be higher in September than in July, when it rose 0.09%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the increase, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says it still expects inflation to fall within its annual target of 1.0% to 3.0% by the end of this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Starting in October, there should be better supply conditions," Mr. Armas said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A survey of 22 analysts released Friday by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed that the consensus for Peru's inflation this year is 3.0%, compared to a consensus of 3.2% in the prior month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's board of directors left its reference interest rate unchanged at 4.25%, where it has stood since May 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BBVA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Banco Continental says it expects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep its policy rate at 4.25% in the coming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "On one hand the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  communique pointed out that inflation is above its target but because of transitory supply-side factors, while output keeps growing close to its potential," the bank said. "On the other, external risks remain high. We expect the policy rate to be left unchanged over the coming months as economic growth close to potential will limit demand-side pressures on prices, while external risks suggest remaining cautious."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics said in a report it sees a "tightening bias" emerging in the next few months. "If global sentiment shows signs of a sustained recovery heading into 2013, the prospect of rate hikes could quickly return to the agenda," the firm said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Peru's economy is expected to grow by about 6.0% this year. In 2011, it expanded by 6.92%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Mr. Armas said the exchange rate between the Peruvian sol and U.S. dollar is expected to continue to depend on global economic factors. So far this year, the sol has strengthened 3.26% against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Armas said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to ease volatility. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to purchase about $9.9 billion so far this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com [ 09-07-12 1525ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120907e897000j8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
