\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Emerging European  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Gain on Euro-Zone, China Optimism\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy  \par \uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2012\par 22:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained, while emerging-market sovereign debt strengthened slightly, as markets pinned their hopes on progress in the euro-zone debt crisis and measures to support China's economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely took cues from European assets, which gained on the back of reports Spain may look to accelerate emergency financial aid for its troubled banking sector. Also Thursday, German Chancellor Angela Merkel also reiterated her country is committed to do what it can to maintain the euro, which help support cheerier market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 "The market is toying with the idea that Europe is moving toward a more reasonable set of policies," said Jose Wynne, head of North America \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in New York. "This is one...step in a very long road, which the market is taking well."\par \par \uc2 Some emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also encouraged by the prospect of more monetary stimulus in the world's second-largest economy, after China's premier said there is growing room for monetary policy measures.\par \par \uc2 Emerging-market sovereign debt strengthened slightly, as investors edged out of haven U.S. Treasurys. The cost for protection on this debt, according to the Markit CDX EM index, tightened to 247 basis points from 249 basis points. Venezuela's sovereign debt, which often outpaces wider market moves, outperformed, as the cost to insure this debt through five-year credit default swaps decreased to 868 basis points from 885 basis points.\par \par \uc2 Among \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , emerging European and African \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were the biggest gainers, spurred by euro-zone optimism and hopes for further China easing.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty advanced more than 1% against the dollar and about 0.6% against the euro, which traded at 4.0554 zlotys, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira advanced modestly, even after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled that it could ease monetary policy in the future. The rate setters, however, kept the interest-rate corridor they use to support the lira and fight inflation unchanged at 5.75% to 11.5%. The lira edged up 0.3% against the dollar, which bought 1.7938 lira late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The South African rand and Nigerian naira were also top gainers. South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped 0.5% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which traded at 8.1962 rand, according to CQG.\par \par \uc2 The naira surged about 1.4% against the dollar, pushed by \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2 's recent announcement that it would include Nigeria in its benchmark index for emerging-market local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt. \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  will add Nigeria to its Government Bond-Emerging Markets Index in three phases beginning October, it said in a research note issued this week. Analysts say Nigeria's expected inclusion could likely spur inflows into the African country's local debt market. On Thursday, the dollar bought 156.55 naira from NGN158.78 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, Peru was in focus after Moody's Investors Service upgraded the country's rating further into investment grade, to Baa2 from Baa3. The ratings firm cited Peru's robust economic growth and sound fiscal performance. The Peruvian sol, however, was little changed on the day, with the dollar trading at 2.614 soles from PEN2.615 late Wednesday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to buy $416 million, as part of its regular efforts to smooth out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  advanced slightly on the back of better-than-expected retail sales data, with the dollar falling 0.2% to buy 2.0189 reais.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its monthly rate-setting meeting later Thursday, but is widely expected to hold its key interest rate at 5%.\par \par \uc2 --Neelabh Chaturvedi, Graciela Ibanez and Nathalie Tadena contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Erin McCarthy at erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 16, 2012 16:28 ET (20:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120816e88g0063p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
