\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2012\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA--Peru's main stock market indexes finished higher Thursday, tracking gains on Wall Street and higher metal prices.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index increased 0.1% to end at 20115.50, while the blue-chip Selective Index gained 0.4% to close at 29379.60.\par \par \uc2 Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 1.1% to end at $37, as copper prices gained. Financial-holding group \uc2 Intergroup Financial Services Corp\uc2  (IFS.VL), which owns Interbank, closed 1% higher at $31.50.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was financial-holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP, BAP.VL), which declined 1.1% to finish at $121.50. Credicorp owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday to buy $164 million at an average of PEN2.6209 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 The sol has been gaining in recent trading sessions due to strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by companies to pay midyear worker bonuses and by consumers for the Independence Day holidays at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed unchanged at PEN2.622 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 07-19-12 1629ET ]\par \par \uc2 Do