\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Finish Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2012\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Wednesday, as shares of a number of mining companies rose on higher metal prices.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's General Index gained 0.27% to end at 20088.64, and the blue-chip Selective Index also rose 0.27% to close at 29272.12.\par \par \uc2 Base-metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) ended 1.59% higher at $32 as copper prices increased, silver and lead miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  (VOLCABC1.VL) rose 0.67% to finish at 3.01 soles ($1.15), and precious-metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl) increased 0.36% to end at $36.62.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday to buy $77 million at an average price of PEN2.6205 per U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 The sol has been gaining in recent trading sessions due to strong demand from companies to pay for midyear-worker bonuses, and from consumers for the Independence Day holidays at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 The sol closed unchanged at PEN2.622 per U.S. dollar Wednesday. So far this year, the sol has appreciated about 2.78% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ryan Dube at ryan.dube@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 07-18-12 1640ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120718e87i000xb\par }\page 