\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2012\par 23:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA -(Dow Jones)- Peru's main stock-market indexes ended higher Thursday, as some blue-chip companies gained while others lost ground.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed 0.59% higher at 20997.56.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index gained 0.4% to finish at 30281.38.\par \par \uc2 Financial-holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP, BAP.VL) closed 2.48% higher at $124.15. Credicorp owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals mining company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl) gained 1.82% to end at $39.20.\par \par \uc2 Posting declines were base-metals mining company \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO, SCCO.VL), which finished 1.59% lower at $28.50.\par \par \uc2 Financial-holding group \uc2 Intergroup Financial Services Corp\uc2  (IFS.VL), which owns Interbank, declined 2.64% to close at $29.50.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to sell $277 million at an average of PEN2.7108 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. This week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $674 million, including Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sol closed weaker Thursday at PEN2.71 to the U.S. dollar, compared to PEN2.706 in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has depreciated 0.48% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945-043-802; peru@dowjones.com [ 05-31-12 1726ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020120531e85v0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
