\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexican peso weakens on U.S. data, labor report eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2012\par 18:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds quotes from Mexico, Peru)\par \par \uc2 * Mexico's peso off 0.5 pct, Brazil's real gains 0.6 pct\par \par \uc2 * U.S. services report creates pessimism ahead of Friday's labor report\par \par \uc2 * Peru raises bank reserve requirements\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 LIMA, May 3 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso weakened on Thursday on disappointing service sector data from the United States, though the real strengthened late in the session after Brazil took a break from market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol weakened slightly as traders digested new bank deposit requirements and Chile's peso closed at its strongest level in more than a month a f ter the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had considered a rate hike at its last board meeting.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Institute for Supply Management said on Thursday its services index fell to 53.5 in April from 56.0 in March, missing economists' forecasts for a modest decline to 55.5.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the report's employment component pointed to lingering weakness in the recovery of the world's largest economy, leading to investor caution ahead of a highly anticipated April labor data scheduled for release on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In response, the Mexican peso weakened 0.5 percent to 12.9991 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is particularly sensitive to U.S. data because Mexico sends nearly 80 percent of its exports to the United States, tying its economy to that of its northern neighbor.\par \par \uc2 "Given the dependency we have with the U.S. economic cycle, in particular with consumption, these signals of weakness are normally related to a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Delia Paredes, director of Analysis at Mexico City brokerage Banorte-IXE in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 "I'm concerned we'll see a contraction of employment in manufacturing in Friday's report," she said.\par \par \uc2 Peru's sol also weakened, closing down 0.08 percent to bid 2.64 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week moved to curb appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by raising some deposit requirements on banks. The sol has traded around its strongest level in 15 years recently, helped by Peru's swift economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "The market continues to feel the impacts of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new measures and one of those is that now dollars are worth more than soles in the bank treasuries," said one trader in Lima who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso meanwhile strengthened 0.48 percent to close bidding 481.8 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest minutes showed that although the bank's governing council voted unanimously to hold the benchmark interest rate at 5.0 percent last month, it considered raising it by 25 basis points.\par \par \uc2 REAL CHANGES COURSE\par \par \uc2 After weakening for much of the session, the real closed 0.64 percent stronger to bid 1.9117 per U.S. dollar as traders cheered less \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 "Two weeks ago we had nearly daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but in the past three days the bank has stayed out of the market, decreasing pressure on the exchange rate," said one trader.\par \par \uc2 The government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have tried to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with taxes on financial transactions and dollar buys in the spot market in a bid to prop up Brazil's manufacturing sector.\par \par \uc2 The real closed at its weakest level since July 2009 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Lower interest rates have also made the real, which has weakened nearly 3 percent this year, less attractive for investors.\par \par \uc2 In the latest sign more rate cuts lie ahead, a draft presidential decree seen by Reuters on Thursday showed President Dilma Rousseff will link returns on some national savings accounts to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lending rate.\par \par \uc2 The proposal carries enormous political and economic risks and amounts to a reengineering of one of the basic pillars of Brazil's financial system.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City, Danielle Fonseca in Sao Paulo and Ursula Scollo in Lima; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120506e8530008p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
