\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  raises deposit rules as sol gains\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2012\par 18:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Stricter rules complement \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soak up inflows\par \par \uc2 * Economic, credit growth stronger than expected\par \par \uc2 * Tighter rules follow 11 months of steady interest rates\par \par \uc2 * Criticism of 'capital controls' resurfaces\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Terry Wade\par \par \uc2 LIMA, April 30 (Reuters) - Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on M onday it was raising deposit requirements on bank accounts in a bid to curb credit expansion and stem appreciation in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is at a 15-year high against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth has been stronger than expected and is forecast to reach 6 percent this year. That has lifted demand for credit, while the sol has firmed about 2 percent since Jan. 1 on heavy inflows of dollars that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has absorbed with frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Abrupt fluctuations in the sol have long concerned officials because about half of Peru's bank deposits are held in dollars and many people and companies earn money in one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but owe debts in the other.\par \par \uc2 "With this package of measures, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeks to act preventively to reduce the rate of growth of liquidity in a context of accelerating de-dollarization of deposits, the greater dollar indebtedness of firms, and low interest rates on dollars - a result of high global liquidity," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Many emerging markets, especially Brazil, have criticized the U.S. Federal Reserve for introducing too much liquidity into the global financial system. Brazil has urged its peers and the IMF to support "defensive" measures designed to fend off excessive appreciation of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The measures in Peru also mean the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after holding its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 4.25 percent for 11 straight months, is adopting a more restrictive monetary stance.\par \par \uc2 Some economists had said the bank was reluctant to raise interest rates to chip away at faster inflation because doing so would have lured in even more hot money.\par \par \uc2 The tighter measures will increase the average deposit rate on bank accounts denominated in soles and U.S. dollars by 0.5 percentage point and boost the marginal deposit rate to 30 percent from 25 percent on accounts denominated in soles.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to discourage inflows of speculative capital, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended to three years from two years the 60 percent deposit requirement that targets short-term credits from abroad. A deposit requirement of 20 percent will also apply to some credits and bonds with terms longer than three years.\par \par \uc2 It was the first time since last April that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed deposit requirements. The new rules take effect on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In 2008, Peruvian officials rejected critics who said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was flirting with capital controls when it raised deposit rules and introduced a commission on a type of money market instrument to curb inflows. Those criticisms resurfaced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The measures suggests that \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  no longer has more ammunition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is now resorting to capital controls," the 4Cast consultancy said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting By Terry Wade, Editing by Leslie Gevirtz and Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 PERU-CENTRALBANK/ (UPDATE 2) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120503e84u0015h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
