\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Peru  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Velarde: Investor, Consumer Confidence Rebounds\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2012\par 18:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:11 EDT *DJ  Peru \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Velarde: Upward Bias In 2012 GDP Forecast\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:15 EDT *DJ  Peru \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Velarde: Still Concerned About Inflation\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:22 EDT *DJ  Peru's Velarde: No Commitment To Any \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Level\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:25 EDT *DJ  Peru's Velarde: Sol Appreciation Not 'Dramatic' This Year\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:32 EDT *DJ  Peru's Velarde: New 2012 GDP Forecast May Be Between 6.0% To 6.2%\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:39 EDT *DJ  Peru's Velarde: Inflation Seen In 1.0% To 3.0% Target This Year\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 12:44 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Velarde: No Short-Term Limits On \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 27 Apr 2012 13:22 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Velarde: Sol Appreciation Not 'Dramatic'\par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Central Reserve Bank of Peru President Julio Velarde said Friday that the appreciation of the sol so far this year hasn't been that "dramatic."\par \par \uc2 Velarde reiterated in a conference call sponsored by the Peruvian Business Council that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have a fixed level for the sol, and added that he wasn't that concerned about the recent appreciation of the sol.\par \par \uc2 The sol has appreciated by 1.97% so far this year against the U.S. dollar and by 6.57% in the last 12-month period.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to purchase dollars and ease the rate at which the sol has appreciated.\par \par \uc2 Velarde said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been sterilizing the inflows of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and added that there are no short-term limits on the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that can be carried out.\par \par \uc2 He also mentioned that in the past, reserve requirements have been used to help manage inflows and said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be able to use that tool again.\par \par \uc2 He said that anyone who believes that the sol will continue to appreciate indefinitely "will be disappointed" at one time or another.\par \par \uc2 Velarde said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official forecast for economic growth for this year is at 5.7% and that there is an upward bias. He added that if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases its forecast that could rise to between 6% to 6.2%.\par \par \uc2 "There are tailwinds that are in our favor," he said, adding that surveys are showing that consumer and investor confidence is returning to levels reached before the general elections held last year.\par \par \uc2 He also pointed to a strong recovery of public sector investments and added that the construction sector is recovering strongly.\par \par \uc2 Velarde added that most analysts now expect the reference interest rate will remain on hold to the end of the year. It has been at 4.25% since May last year.\par \par \uc2 He said that inflation, while still a concern, is expected to end this year within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 1% to 3%.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 27, 2012 13:22 ET (17:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120427e84r005np\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
