\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  gains after Dutch debt sale\b0\par\par\uc2 509 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2012\par 18:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real gains 0.25 pct, Mexico's peso up 0.15 pct\par \par \uc2 * Dutch bond sale eases Euro-zone concerns\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  sol heads for new 15-year high, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  eyed\par \par \uc2 By Caroline Stauffer\par \par \uc2 Lima, April 24 (Reuters) - Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on Tuesday after a debt auction in Holland eased concerns over the European crisis and positive news in U.S. consumer confidence and housing reports supported modest gains.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso gained 0.15 percent to 13.1573, recovering from its weakest level in three months. Brazil's real\par \par \uc2 strengthened 0.25 percent to bid 1.8763 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Investors breathed a sigh of relief after the Dutch state raised 2 billion euros by selling two bonds at an auction. The prime minister's resignation over budget cuts on Monday had raised concerns the European debt crisis could be spreading.\par \par \uc2 "I've seen a strong relationship between the (Mexican) peso and risk sentiment coming from Europe," said Alfredo Puig, a trader at Vector brokerage in Monterrey. "Today's placements helped us, the Dutch auction was very important."\par \par \uc2 Data from the United States, Mexico's top trading partner, showed new U.S. single-family home sales dropped in March but the reading still beat analysts' expectations.\par \par \uc2 The S&P/Case-Shiller housing report meanwhile showed U.S. single-family home prices rose in February for the first time in 10 months in a sign the sector is starting to stabilize.\par \par \uc2 "All of this is supporting U.S. stocks, and Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are following that," said Pedro Tuesta, an economist with Washington-based 4Cast.\par \par \uc2 Signs of recovery in the world's largest economy support assets perceived as risky, like stocks and emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Farther south, Chile's peso gained 0.28 percent to bid 487 per dollar. Peru's sol gained 0.04 percent to bid 2.65 per dollar, heading for its strongest close in some 15 years, though traders said that level provoked caution.\par \par \uc2 "Breaking the 2.65 barrier will cause an official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there's hardly any trading," said one Lima-based trader who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought dollars on the spot market nearly every day in recent weeks amid heavy dollar inflows and strong economic growth in the Andean country.\par \par \uc2 Though Brazil's real gained on Tuesday, it is the worst performer this month of the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Thomson Reuters. Investors have bet against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to weaken it.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  said in a report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains an attractive carry trade investment even though it is not likely to strengthen beyond 1.8 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Hindsight has shown that sell-offs like these have proven excellent medium-term opportunities," the brokerage said.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Ursula Scolo in Lima; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120427e84o001qp\par }\