\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Sol Seen Appreciating More Than Earlier Forecast\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2012\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Economists revise forecasts for stronger sol at end of 2012\par \par \uc2 --The sol has appreciated 1.56% so far this year, despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchases in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market close in on record from 2007\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Ryan Dube \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The strengthening of Peru's sol in the first months of this year has led some economists to revise their forecasts for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's year-end exchange rate against the U.S. dollar, projecting that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate more in 2012 than previously anticipated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Over the last several years, the sol has benefited from strong inflows of foreign direct investments, which have been attracted to the Andean country thanks to its political and fiscal stability. In 2011, the sol strengthened 4% against the dollar, and has appreciated about 14% since the end of 2008.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far this year, the trend has continued. On Wednesday, the sol closed at PEN2.655 per dollar, 1.56% stronger than its closing rate at the end of last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hedmond Rios, an economist with brokerage Celfin Capital, told Dow Jones Newswires on Wednesday that he recently revised his year-end forecast for the sol and now expects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to close 2012 at PEN2.64 per dollar, compared to a previous forecast of PEN2.68 per dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to continue its appreciation trend," Rios said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banco de Credito del Peru\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the country's largest bank, also recently revised its year-end forecast for the sol. The bank is forecasting that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will appreciate 3% in 2012 to finish at PEN2.62, compared to a previous projection of PEN2.64.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banco de Credito\f28 \uc2 \f2 's chief economist, Alonso Segura, said during a meeting with reporters on Tuesday that there is a "downward bias" in the forecast, indicating that the sol could strengthen beyond the bank's official projection.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said he hasn't seen "anything that changes the tendency" for the sol's appreciation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Central Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to reduce volatility. So far this year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has bought about $7 billion, which is more than all of 2011, and is closing in on its 2007 record, when it bought $10.3 billion in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mario Guerrero, an economist with Scotiabank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the country's third-largest bank, said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should continue, however with "less intensity" as seasonal factors that affected the exchange rate ease.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Officials from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have said that the sol's appreciation this year has been strongly affected by seasonal factors, including increased demand for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by mining companies to pay local taxes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We should see the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continue to buy dollars, but I think in less intensity than in the first months of this year," said Guerrero. He projects the sol will end 2012 at PEN2.63 per dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ryan Dube, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-945 043 802; peru@dowjones.com [ 18-04-12 2018GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120418e84i00161\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
