\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Broad General Stock Index Ends At Record High\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2012\par 22:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Peru's main stock index ends at record high\par \par \uc2 --General Index breaches level last reached in July 2007\par \par \uc2 --Stock market driven by improved external conditions, commodities\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Robert Kozak \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA, Peru (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market index ended at a record high Monday, breaching a level the broad General Index last reached almost five years ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Optimism about external markets and strong domestic demand have helped propel the main indexes on the Lima Stock Exchange.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is optimism" among investors, said Edwin Paz, a trader with brokerage Provalor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday, the Lima Stock Exchange's General Index closed 1.86% higher at 24051.62.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The previous record, reached in mid-July 2007, was 23789, but then the stock market weakened due mainly to global financial and economic problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday, the blue-chip Selective Index ended 1.91% higher at 33913.37.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Peru's stock market more recently has followed other bourses higher, while improved commodity prices have given a large boost to indexes in Peru, which are heavily weighted in mining companies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The perception of improved optimism in external markets has benefited, above all, shares related with economic growth in the nation. Investors have bet on a rise in shares linked to domestic demand," Scotiabank said in a report.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that it expects Peru's economy to expand by 6.5% this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday, financial holding company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credicorp Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (BAP) rose 2.10% to end at $133.90. The company owns Peru's largest bank.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Precious metals mining concern \f28 \uc2 \f2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\f28 \uc2 \f2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl) gained 2.12% to end at $41.00 as the price of gold improved.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tin mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Minsur SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MINSURI1.VL) increased 4.10% to end at 3.30 soles, ($1.24) on a rise in tin prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Central Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday to buy $75 million at an average of PEN2.6678 per U.S. dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought about $5.5 billion in the first three months of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the sol closed slightly stronger Monday at PEN2.668 per U.S. dollar, compared with PEN2.669 per dollar in the previous session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 1.08% against the greenback.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 04-02-12 1640ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020120402e8420004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
