\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 21:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Monday, as a number of key blue chip shares gained ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed 0.51% stronger at 23,079.77.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.59% higher at 32,153.24.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) increased 1.09% to end at $32.33, as the price of copper improved.\par \par \uc2 Tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) gained 0.33% to end at 3.06 soles, ($1.35) on a rise in tin prices.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) rose 0.55% to end at $127.50. It owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 "It is possible that the General Index will resume its upward trend in the short term," Scotiabank said in a report.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to buy $48 million at an average of 2.6708 Peruvian soles per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 So far this year to March 13 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase a net $4.74 billion. That has helped lift Peru's net international reserves to $54.77 billion as of March 13.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed slightly weaker Monday at PEN2.672 per dollar, compared with PEN2.671 per dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has strengthened 0.93% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 03-19-12 1614ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020120319e83j0004z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
