\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  And Debt Gain On Liquidity Boost\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 21:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt gained modestly Thursday.\par \par \uc2 While several factors drove individual \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , global sentiment was dominated by continued uncertainty about the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's intentions over a third round of quantitative easing and the expectation of more capital flows into emerging market assets following the recent round of loans to European banks.\par \par \uc2 While manufacturing data from Asian countries was mixed, China's rise in production was viewed with relief. Another source of good news was Poland's unexpected 4.3% increase in gross domestic product in the fourth quarter, at a time when the European sovereign debt crisis was going through its worst convulsion. This sent the euro, quoted in zloty, to PLN4.0992. It recently traded at PLN4.1033, according to CQG data. Analysts expect investors to pick up the zloty, in preference to its neighbors--the Hungarian forint and the Czech koruna--both of which have benefited from broader improvement in investor confidence.\par \par \uc2 Not all central banks, however, are comfortable with the appreciation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Brazil took another step in combating the rapid appreciation of the real and extended a 6% tax on foreign loans of up to three years to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. This helped weaken the real, with the dollar quoted at BRL1.7266. But that quickly faded and the dollar recently traded at BRL1.7121.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants worry that continued focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness could trigger inflation. Other Latin American countries like \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, to curb its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility. The dollar recently traded flat at 2.675 soles.\par \par \uc2 A few analysts are urging investors to get into the Mexican peso now, as that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again seems to be at the cusp of a rally. The Mexican economy is expected to grow rapidly on the back of the recovery in the U.S. economy and its oil resources at a time when oil prices are once again on the rise.\par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  analysts say they favor the Mexican peso, South African rand and the Polish zloty, and the Philippines peso and Korean won among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Emerging market debt, meanwhile, performed strongly as reflected by the nine basis points narrowing of the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Global to 347 basis points over comparable Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 -By Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com [ 01-03-12 2052GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120301e8310019i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
