\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2012\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended slightly lower Wednesday, as a number of smaller companies lost ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed 0.01% weaker, at 22,870.86.\par \par \uc2 The blue-chip Selective Index ended 0.02% lower, at 31,532.96.\par \par \uc2 Silver and lead miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) fell 0.28%, to end at 3.50 soles ($1.19) in heavy volume.\par \par \uc2 Peru's largest cement producer, \uc2 Cementos Lima SA\uc2  (CEMLIMI1.VL), lost 0.37%, to end at PEN2.67.\par \par \uc2 Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA (BROCALC1.VL), one of Peru's leading silver producers, declined 0.10%, to end at PEN51.00.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday to buy $133 million at an average of PEN2.680 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the sol closed unchanged at PEN2.681 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 0.59% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 02-22-12 1629ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 27   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020120222e82m0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
